# Setup Instructions

Copy mr_seq_test.ex and the tests folder (with all subfolders) to the directory containing your mrseq.ex implementation.

Ensure word_count.ex and indexer.ex are in the same directory.

Start the Elixir interpreter:
   iex

Verify the interpreter's current working directory contains mrseq.ex and the above files.

Compile the test file and your implementation:
   c ["mr_seq_test.ex", "mrseq.ex"]

Import the test module:
   import MRSeqTest


## Running Tests

Run all tests:
   test_all

Run an individual test:
For example, to run test_long_7 with the word count script:
   test_fun.test_long_7.("word_count.ex")

The complete list of individual tests is available in the test_fun function. Test names are self-explanatory (the integer indicates the number of input splits).

Run all word count tests:
   test_wc

Run all indexer tests:
   test_ind


## Checking Results

Model outputs for each test case are located in tests/test_out.

If a test fails, use the diff command to compare your output with the model output.
